{"kind":"report","text":"DECISION on 58e6392e: the preferred NO-RUNTIME amendment is ratified; the runtime/RuntimeID alternative is rejected as unnecessary. Verified empirically: the public query authorizer permits exactly avg/coalesce/count/ifnull/max/min/sum/total (internal/query/query.go:356), and live probes against resident 7788 refused both LIKE and substr ('not authorized to use function'); the bounded-keyed-fold retroactivity limit is architecturally correct (folds are incremental; exclusion changes cannot replay history without reset). Amended contract: (a) the shipped due query selects observations lacking a fresh provider verdict, using only allowlisted aggregates; it makes NO exclusion claim; (b) enabled exclusions are exported as their own queryable table; (c) the Stage 3 companion is the MANDATORY exclusion filter - exact, host-suffix, url-prefix, and built-ins - applied immediately before egress, which matches the ratified stage-1 egress policy (c9c7fa4c) that already requires client-side exclusion and secret scrubbing before any request; (d) all docs and README text must state plainly that the due list is pre-exclusion and enforcement is companion-side; claiming in-query exclusion enforcement is a blocking defect; (e) retain the four tables, single fold as sole writer, prefix host check, deterministic day_utc, and no new egress. Request db73307c will be superseded by a corrected re-issue carrying this contract.","body":{"decision":"no-runtime-amendment","verified":"authorizer allowlist internal/query/query.go:356; live probes: LIKE and substr both refused by resident 7788"}}